-- title:
--   Level polynomials for the modular unit on X₁(Mp)
-- statement:
--   Let $p$ be a prime, $M \ge 5$ a nonzero natural number with $p \nmid M$, and let $L$ be a field of characteristic zero which is a cyclotomic extension of $\mathbb{Q}$ for $\{p\}$, with $\zeta \in L$ a primitive $p$-th root of unity. Let $K$ be the intermediate field of $\mathrm{LaurentSeries}\,L$ over $L$ obtained by adjoining to $L$ the image, under the coefficientwise map $\mathrm{coeffEmb}\,L$ induced by $\mathbb{Q} \to L$, of the $q$-expansion function field of $\Gamma_1(Mp)$ over $\mathbb{Q}$. Let $A$ be a discrete valuation domain with fraction field $L$ such that $p$ lies in the maximal ideal of $A$ and $\zeta$ is in the image of $A$, together with an $A$-algebra structure on $K$ compatible with $A \to L \to K$. Let $j \in K$ be nonzero with Laurent series the image of the $q$-expansion $q^{-1}\cdot jNumQ$ of the modular invariant, and write $\mathrm{chartAlgFin}\,A\,K\,j$ for the subalgebra of elements of $K$ integral over $A[j]$. Let $v$ be an element of this subalgebra whose Laurent series is either the image of the modular unit series $\Delta(q)/\Delta(q^p)$ or $p^{12}$ times the inverse of that image. Then, for any natural numbers $A_0, B_0, n_0$, there are naturals $b$ and $M_b$ with $A_0 b^{n_0} + B_0 < M_b$, a family $g : \mathrm{Fin}\,M_b \to \mathbb{Z}[X]$ of monic polynomials and ranks $\mathrm{rk} : \mathrm{Fin}\,M_b \to \mathbb{N}$ such that for every $i$ the quotient of $\mathrm{chartAlgFin}\,A\,K\,j$ by the ideal generated by $g_i(v)$ is a finite, étale and free $A$-algebra of $A$-rank $\mathrm{rk}\,i$, with $1 \le \mathrm{rk}\,i \le b$, the ideals $(g_i(v))$ are pairwise comaximal, and each $(g_i(v))$ is comaximal with $(v)$.
--
--   The statement produces, on the chart algebra of the two-chart model of $X_1(Mp)$ over a discrete valuation ring containing $\zeta_p$, arbitrarily many level sets of the modular unit $\Delta(q)/\Delta(q^p)$ (or of its normalised inverse) that are finite étale and free over the base, of bounded rank, pairwise disjoint and disjoint from the divisor of the unit itself; the number of such level sets exceeds any prescribed polynomial bound $A_0 b^{n_0} + B_0$ in the rank bound $b$. It feeds the construction of a one-sided pool inside the smooth locus of the model.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_XOneP_exists_levelPolynomials_chartAlgFin_twoChartModel_x1_mul.lean

